      "answer": "Gupta Empire",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The period of peace under Kushan rule is known as Pax Kushana.  By the 3rd century, their empire in India was disintegrating and their last known great emperor was Vasudeva I.  === Classical period (c.  320 – 650 CE) === ==== Gupta Empire ==== The Gupta period was noted for cultural creativity, especially in literature, architecture, sculpture, and painting.  The Gupta period produced scholars such as Kalidasa, Aryabhata, Varahamihira, Vishnu Sharma, and Vatsyayana.  The Gupta period marked a watershed of Indian culture: the Guptas performed Vedic sacrifices to legitimise their rule, but they also patronised Buddhism, an alternative to Brahmanical orthodoxy.  The military exploits of the first three rulers – Chandragupta I, Samudragupta, and Chandragupta II – brought much of India under their leadership"
    },
