      "fact": " 655–900 CE) and Kamarupa-Palas (c.  900–1100 CE), from their capitals in present-day Guwahati (Pragjyotishpura), Tezpur (Haruppeswara) and North Gauhati (Durjaya) respectively.  All three dynasties claimed their descent from Narakasura.  In the reign of the Varman king, Bhaskar Varman (c.  600–650 CE), the Chinese traveller Xuanzang visited the region and recorded his travels.  Later, after weakening and disintegration (after the Kamarupa-Palas), the Kamarupa tradition was somewhat extended until c.  1255 CE by the Lunar I (c"
