      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Indian History",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:27:18.214Z",
      "subject": "Indian History",
      "subSubject": "History of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "=== _____ === The Delhi Sultanate was a series of successive Islamic states based in Delhi, ruled by several dynasties of varying origins",
      "answer": "Delhi Sultanate",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " This was an important period in the development of fine arts in Southern India, especially in literature as the Western Chalukya kings encouraged writers in the native language of Kannada, and Sanskrit like the philosopher and statesman Basava and the great mathematician Bhāskara II.  == Late medieval period (c.  1200 – 1526) == The late medieval period is marked by repeated invasions by Muslim Central Asian nomadic clans, the rule of the Delhi Sultanate, and by the growth of other states, built upon military technology of the sultanate.  === Delhi Sultanate === The Delhi Sultanate was a series of successive Islamic states based in Delhi, ruled by several dynasties of varying origins.  The polity ruled over large parts of the Indian subcontinent from the 13th to early 16th centuries.  The sultanate was founded in the 12th and 13th centuries by Central Asian Turks, who invaded parts of northern India and established the state atop former Hindu holdings.  The subsequent Mamluk dynasty of Delhi managed to conquer large areas of northern India"
    },
