      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Maratha–Mysore War ended in April 1787, following the finalising of treaty of Gajendragad, in which Tipu Sultan was obligated to pay tribute to the Marathas.  Concurrently, the Anglo-Mysore Wars took place, where the Mysoreans used the Mysorean rockets.  The Fourth Anglo-Mysore War (1798–1799) saw the death of Tipu.  Mysore's alliance with the French was seen as a threat to the British East India Company, and Mysore was attacked from all four sides.  The Nizam of Hyderabad and the Marathas launched an invasion from the north.  The British won a decisive victory at the Siege of Seringapatam (1799).  Hyderabad was founded by the Qutb Shahi dynasty of Golconda in 1591"
