      "answer": "Jagannath Temple",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The British forces managed to stop the armies of the allies, forcing Chinnamalai to attack Coimbatore on his own.  His army was defeated and he escaped from the British forces.  Chinnamalai engaged in guerrilla warfare and defeated the British in battles at Cauvery in 1801, Odanilai in 1802 and Arachalur in 1804.  In 1804 the King of Khordha, Kalinga was deprived of his traditional rights to the Jagannath Temple.  In retaliation, a group of armed Paiks attacked the British at Pipili.  Jayee Rajguru, the chief of Army of Kalinga requested a common alliance against the British.  After Rajguru's death, Bakshi Jagabandhu launched an armed revolution against the East India Company's rule in Odisha"
