      "answer": "Lal Bal Pal",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The work of men like Swami Vivekananda, Ramakrishna, Sri Aurobindo, V.  Chidambaram Pillai, Subramanya Bharathy, Bankim Chandra Chatterjee, Rabindranath Tagore and Dadabhai Naoroji, as well as women such as the Scots–Irish Sister Nivedita, spread the passion for rejuvenation and freedom.  The rediscovery of India's indigenous history by several European and Indian scholars also fed into the rise of nationalism among Indians.  The triumvirate also is known as Lal Bal Pal (Bal Gangadhar Tilak, Bipin Chandra Pal, Lala Lajpat Rai), along with V.  Chidambaram Pillai, Sri Aurobindo, Surendranath Banerjee, and Rabindranath Tagore were some of the prominent leaders of movements in the early 20th century.  The Swadeshi movement was the most successful.  The name of Lokmanya began spreading around and people started following him in all parts of the country"
    },
    {
      "id": "q443",
      "type": "fill_blank",
