      "question": "_____, a veteran Congressman and Indian leader, became Gandhi's mentor",
      "answer": "Gopal Krishna Gokhale",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Gandhi accomplished this through extensive use of non-violent protests, such as boycotting, protest marching, and fasting by him and his followers.  Gandhi returned to India on 9 January 1915, and initially entered the political fray not with calls for a nation-state, but in support of the unified commerce-oriented territory that the Congress Party had been asking for.  Gandhi believed that the industrial development and educational development that the Europeans had brought were long required to alleviate many of India's chronic problems.  Gopal Krishna Gokhale, a veteran Congressman and Indian leader, became Gandhi's mentor.  Gandhi's ideas and strategies of non-violent civil disobedience initially appeared impractical to some Indians and their Congress leaders.  In the Mahatma's own words, \"civil disobedience is civil breach of immoral statutory enactments. \" It had to be carried out non-violently by withdrawing co-operation with the corrupt state"
