      "hint": "",
      "fact": " American policymakers, including Kennan and John Foster Dulles, acknowledged that the Cold War was in its essence a war of ideas.  The United States, acting through the CIA, funded a long list of projects to counter the communist appeal among intellectuals in Europe and the developing world.  The CIA also covertly sponsored a domestic propaganda campaign called Crusade for Freedom.  === German rearmament === The rearmament of West Germany was achieved in the early 1950s.  Its main promoter was Konrad Adenauer, the chancellor of West Germany, with France the main opponent.  Washington had the decisive voice.  It was strongly supported by the Pentagon (the US military leadership), and weakly opposed by President Truman; the State Department was ambivalent"
