      "question": "Bush and Gorbachev met at the _____ in May 1988 and the Governors Island Summit in December 1988",
      "answer": "Moscow Summit",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The INF treaty eliminated all nuclear-armed, ground-launched ballistic and cruise missiles with ranges between 500 and 5,500 kilometers (310 and 3,420 mi) and their infrastructure.  During 1988, it became apparent to the Soviets that oil and gas subsidies, along with the cost of maintaining massive troops levels, represented a substantial economic drain.  In addition, the security advantage of a buffer zone was recognized as irrelevant and the Soviets officially declared that they would no longer intervene in the affairs of satellite states in Central and Eastern Europe.  Bush and Gorbachev met at the Moscow Summit in May 1988 and the Governors Island Summit in December 1988.  In 1989, Soviet forces withdrew from Afghanistan without achieving their objectives.  Later that year, the Berlin Wall, the Inner German border and the Iron Curtain fell.  On 3 December 1989, Gorbachev and Bush declared the Cold War over at the Malta Summit"
