      "answer": "Although Soviet",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Cold War also marked the zenith of peacetime military–industrial complexes and large-scale military funding of science.  Cumulative US military expenditures throughout the entire Cold War amounted to an estimated $8 trillion.  Nearly 100,000 Americans died in the Korean and Vietnam Wars.  Although Soviet casualties are difficult to estimate, as a share of gross national product the financial cost for the Soviet Union was much higher than that incurred by the United States.  Millions died in the superpowers' proxy wars around the globe, most notably in eastern Asia.  Most of the proxy wars and subsidies for local conflicts ended along with the Cold War; interstate wars, ethnic wars, revolutionary wars, as well as refugee and displaced persons crises have declined sharply in the post-Cold War years.  The aftermath of the Cold War is, however, not considered to be concluded"
    },
