      "question": "Conservatives across Europe called for the destruction of revolutionary France, and in February the Convention responded by declaring war on Britain and the _____",
      "answer": "Dutch Republic",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " On 17 January 1793, Louis was sentenced to death for \"conspiracy against public liberty and general safety\".  361 deputies were in favour, 288 against, while another 72 voted to execute him, subject to delaying conditions.  The sentence was carried out on 21 January on the Place de la Révolution, now the Place de la Concorde.  Conservatives across Europe called for the destruction of revolutionary France, and in February the Convention responded by declaring war on Britain and the Dutch Republic.  Together with Austria and Prussia, these two countries were later joined by Spain, Portugal, Naples, and Tuscany in the War of the First Coalition.  === Political crisis and fall of the Girondins === The Girondins hoped war would unite the people behind the government and provide an excuse for rising prices and food shortages.  Instead, they found themselves the target of popular anger and in what proved a disastrous strategic move, many left Paris for the provinces"
    },
    {
