      "question": "Padhye, introduced this form of puppetry to India in the 1920s and his son, _____, subsequently popularised ventriloquism and puppetry",
      "answer": "Ramdas Padhye",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In the ancient Indian epic Mahabharata there are references to puppets.  Kathputli, a form of string puppet performance native to Rajasthan, is notable and there are many Indian ventriloquists and puppeteers.  The first Indian ventriloquist, Professor Y.  Padhye, introduced this form of puppetry to India in the 1920s and his son, Ramdas Padhye, subsequently popularised ventriloquism and puppetry.  Ramdas Padhye's son, Satyajit Padhye is also a ventriloquist and puppeteer.  Almost all types of puppets are found in India.  String puppets India has a rich and ancient tradition of string puppets or marionettes"
