      "question": "_____ in Mumbai, Mysore Palace has on display a few good Indian paintings",
      "answer": "Jehangir Art Gallery",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Venkatappa are some modern painters.  Among the present-day artists, Atul Dodiya, Bose Krishnamacnahri, Devajyoti Ray and Shibu Natesan represent a new era of Indian art where global art shows direct amalgamation with Indian classical styles.  These recent artists have acquired international recognition.  Jehangir Art Gallery in Mumbai, Mysore Palace has on display a few good Indian paintings.  === Sculpture === The first sculptures in India date back to the Indus Valley civilisation, where stone and bronze figures have been discovered.  Later, as Hinduism, Buddhism, and Jainism developed further, India produced some extremely intricate bronzes as well as temple carvings.  Some huge shrines, such as the one at Ellora were not constructed by using blocks but carved out of solid rock"
