    {
      "id": "q1168",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Art & Culture",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:27:41.677Z",
      "subject": "Art & Culture",
      "subSubject": "Culture of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "The modern game of polo is derived from Manipur, India, where the game was known as '_____', 'Kanjai-bazee', or 'Pulu'",
      "answer": "Sagol Kangjei",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Chess is commonly believed to have originated in northwestern India during the Gupta empire, where its early form in the 6th century was known as chaturanga.  Other games which originated in India and continue to remain popular in wide parts of northern India include Kabaddi, Gilli-Danda, and Kho kho.  Traditional southern Indian games include Snake boat race and Kuttiyum kolum.  The modern game of polo is derived from Manipur, India, where the game was known as 'Sagol Kangjei', 'Kanjai-bazee', or 'Pulu'.  It was the anglicised form of the last, referring to the wooden ball that was used, which was adopted by the sport in its slow spread to the west.  The first polo club was established in the town of Silchar in Assam, India, in 1833.  In 2011, India inaugurated a privately built Buddh International Circuit, its first motor racing circuit"
    },
    {
      "id": "q1169",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Art & Culture",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:27:41.677Z",
      "subject": "Art & Culture",
      "subSubject": "Culture of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "In 2011, India inaugurated a privately built _____, its first motor racing circuit",
      "answer": "Buddh International Circuit",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The modern game of polo is derived from Manipur, India, where the game was known as 'Sagol Kangjei', 'Kanjai-bazee', or 'Pulu'.  It was the anglicised form of the last, referring to the wooden ball that was used, which was adopted by the sport in its slow spread to the west.  The first polo club was established in the town of Silchar in Assam, India, in 1833.  In 2011, India inaugurated a privately built Buddh International Circuit, its first motor racing circuit. 14-kilometre circuit is in Greater Noida, Uttar Pradesh, near Delhi.  The first Formula One Indian Grand Prix event was hosted here in October 2011.  === Indian martial arts === One of the best known forms of ancient Indian martial arts is the Kalarippayattu from Kerala"
    },
    {
