      "subSubject": "Constitution of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "26 November _____: The Constitution of India was passed and adopted by the assembly",
      "answer": "1949",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Gopalaswami Ayyangar, Devi Prasad Khaitan and BL Mitter.  16 July 1948: Along with Harendra Coomar Mookerjee, V.  Krishnamachari was also elected as second vice-president of Constituent Assembly.  26 November 1949: The Constitution of India was passed and adopted by the assembly.  24 January 1950: Last meeting of Constituent Assembly.  The Constitution was signed and accepted (with 395 Articles, 8 Schedules, and 22 Parts).  26 January 1950: The Constitution came into force"
    },
    {
      "id": "q1255",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Polity",
      "region": "",
