      "fact": " Judges, such as Alladi Krishnaswamy Iyer, Benegal Narsing Rau, K.  Munshi and Ganesh Mavlankar were members of the assembly.  Female members included Sarojini Naidu, Hansa Mehta, Durgabai Deshmukh, Amrit Kaur and Vijaya Lakshmi Pandit.  The first, two-day president of the assembly was Sachchidananda Sinha; Rajendra Prasad was later elected president.  It met for the first time on 9 December 1946.  === Drafting === Sir B.  Rau, a civil servant who became the first Indian judge in the International Court of Justice and was president of the United Nations Security Council, was appointed as the assembly's constitutional advisor in 1946"
