      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:28:09.484Z",
      "subject": "Polity",
      "subSubject": "Politics of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "==== Types of political parties ==== Every political party in India, whether a national or regional/state party, must have a symbol and must be registered with the _____ of India",
      "answer": "Election Commission",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " It has been estimated that over 200 parties were formed after India became independent in 1947.  As per latest publications dated 23 March 2024 from Election Commission of India, and subsequent notifications, there are 6 national parties, 57 state parties, and 2,764 registered unrecognized parties.  All registered parties contesting elections need to choose a symbol from a list of available symbols offered by the EC.  ==== Types of political parties ==== Every political party in India, whether a national or regional/state party, must have a symbol and must be registered with the Election Commission of India.  Symbols are used in the Indian political system to identify political parties in part so that illiterate people can vote by recognizing the party symbols.  In the current amendment to the Symbols Order, the commission has asserted the following five principles: A party, national or state, must have a legislative presence.  A national party's legislative presence must be in the Lok Sabha"
    },
