      "emoji": "",
      "question": "In the current amendment to the _____, the commission has asserted the following five principles: A party, national or state, must have a legislative presence",
      "answer": "Symbols Order",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " All registered parties contesting elections need to choose a symbol from a list of available symbols offered by the EC.  ==== Types of political parties ==== Every political party in India, whether a national or regional/state party, must have a symbol and must be registered with the Election Commission of India.  Symbols are used in the Indian political system to identify political parties in part so that illiterate people can vote by recognizing the party symbols.  In the current amendment to the Symbols Order, the commission has asserted the following five principles: A party, national or state, must have a legislative presence.  A national party's legislative presence must be in the Lok Sabha.  A state party's legislative presence must be in the State Assembly.  A party can set up a candidate only from amongst its own members"
    },
