      "answer": "Fitch Ratings",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " === COVID-19 pandemic and new reforms (2021–present) === During the COVID-19 pandemic, numerous rating agencies downgraded India's GDP predictions for FY21 to negative figures, signalling a recession in India, the most severe since 1979.  The Indian Economy contracted by 6. 6 percent which was lower than the estimated 7.  In 2022, the ratings agency Fitch Ratings upgraded India's outlook to stable similar to S&P Global Ratings and Moody's Investors Service's outlooks.  In the first quarter of financial year 2022–2023, the Indian economy grew by 13.  With 607 million workers, India has the world's second-largest labour force, which is growing rapidly, with 46. 6 million added in 2023–24 alone"
