      "fact": " The collision with the Eurasian Plate along the modern border between India and Nepal formed the orogenic belt that created the Tibetan Plateau and the Himalayas.  As of 2009, the Indian Plate is moving northeast at 5 cm/yr (2 in/yr), while the Eurasian Plate is moving north at only 2 cm/yr (0.  India is thus referred to as the \"fastest continent\".  This is causing the Eurasian Plate to deform, and the Indian Plate to compress at a rate of 4 cm/yr (1.  == Political geography == India is divided into 28 States (further subdivided into districts) and 8 union territories including the National capital territory (i.  India's borders run a total length of 15,200 km (9,400 mi).  Its borders with Pakistan and Bangladesh were delineated according to the Radcliffe Line, which was created in 1947 during Partition of India"
    },
