      "fact": " Temperatures are around 35 °C (95 °F) but humidity is very high; nights are around 27 °C (81 °F).  Most of the rainfall occurs in this season, and the rain can cause severe floods.  The sun is often occluded during the monsoon season.  East of the Thar Desert, the Southwest Punjab–West Haryana–Kathiawar region experiences a tropical and sub-tropical steppe climate.  Haryana's climate resembles other states of the northern plains: extreme summer heat of up to 45 °C (113 °F) and winter cold as low as 0 °C (32 °F).  May and June are hottest; December and January are coldest.  Rainfall is varied, with the Shivalik Hills region being the wettest and the Bagar region being the driest"
    },
