      "emoji": "",
      "question": "However, parts of _____, Orissa, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka and Mumbai also receive minor precipitation from the north-east monsoon",
      "answer": "West Bengal",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " It carries winds that have already lost their moisture out to the ocean (opposite from the summer monsoon).  They cross India diagonally from northeast to southwest.  However, the large indentation made by the Bay of Bengal into India's eastern coast means that the flows are humidified before reaching Cape Comorin and rest of Tamil Nadu, meaning that the state, and also some parts of Kerala, experience significant precipitation in the post-monsoon and winter periods.  However, parts of West Bengal, Orissa, Andhra Pradesh, Karnataka and Mumbai also receive minor precipitation from the north-east monsoon.  == Statistics == Shown below are temperature and precipitation data for selected Indian cities; these represent the full variety of major Indian climate types.  Figures have been grouped by the four-season classification scheme used by the Indian Meteorological Department; year-round averages and totals are also displayed.  === Temperature === === Precipitation === == Disasters == Climate-related natural disasters cause massive losses of Indian life and property"
