      "hint": "",
      "fact": " 60 flies with the INAS 300 and INAS 552 squadrons of the Indian Navy.  The Mikoyan MiG-29K will be deployed aboard INS Vikramaditya.  The Indian Navy operates five Il-38 planes.  They are being upgraded to use the Sea Dragon suite.  Used principally for anti-submarine warfare (ASW) and search and rescue roles, the helicopter fleet of Westland Sea King and the Sikorsky SH-3 Sea King operate from INS Garuda (Kochi) as well as INS Kunjali-II (Mumbai) air stations.  56 more naval utility helicopters are planned to be inducted from 2016.  These will be used for surveillance, anti-submarine warfare, electronic intelligence gathering, and search and rescue operations"
