      "subSubject": "Indian Armed Forces",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "The DRDO is also going ahead with its plans to develop a new class of UAV, referred to by the HALE (_____) and MALE (Medium Altitude Long Endurance) designations",
      "answer": "High Altitude Long Endurance",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " === Unmanned Aerial Vehicles === The DRDO has also developed many unmanned aerial vehicles- such as the Nishant tactical UAV and the Lakshya Pilotless Target Aircraft (PTA).  The Lakshya PTA has been ordered by all three services for their gunnery target training requirements.  Efforts are ongoing to develop the PTA further, with an improved all-digital flight control system and a better turbojet engine.  The DRDO is also going ahead with its plans to develop a new class of UAV, referred to by the HALE (High Altitude Long Endurance) and MALE (Medium Altitude Long Endurance) designations.  The MALE UAV has been tentatively named the Rustom, and will feature canards and carry a range of payloads, including optronic, radar, laser designators, and ESM.  The UAV will have conventional landing and take-off capability.  The HALE UAV will have features such as SATCOM links, allowing it to be commanded beyond line of sight"
    },
