      "subSubject": "Indian Armed Forces",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "Kohli led the _____'s first successful expedition to Mount Everest in 1965",
      "answer": "Indian Navy",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " With the weather being clear at such altitudes and coordinates planned by the IAF pilots, both the AN-32 and Mirage-2000 pilots were able to accomplish the mission.  === Indian Navy exploration === The Indian Navy regularly conducts adventure expeditions.  The sailing ship and training vessel INS Tarangini began circumnavigating the world on 23 January 2003, intending to foster good relations with other nations; she returned to India in May of the following year after visiting 36 ports in 18 nations.  Kohli led the Indian Navy's first successful expedition to Mount Everest in 1965.  Another Navy team also successfully scaled Everest from the north face, the more technically challenging route.  An Indian Navy team comprising 11 members completed an expedition to the North Pole in 2006.  The Indian Naval ensign first flew in Antarctica in 1981"
