      "hint": "",
      "fact": " == Recruitment and Training == === Officers (Permanent commission) === ==== National Defence Academy and Naval Academy Examination ==== The NDA/NA is the premier entry route to join the army as Permanent Commission officers.  It is open to unmarried candidates aged 16½–19½ years, NDA/NA selects students after 10+2, irrespective of stream for army.  The NDA/NA exam is held twice a year, consisting of Mathematics and General Ability.  Candidates who clear the cutoff undergo a five-day Services Selection Board (SSB) interview, followed by a medical examination.  The final merit determines the selection.  The examination is highly competitive as approximately 600,000 candidates apply for roughly 800 vacancies each year.  Training is conducted in two phases"
