      "question": "== Environmentalism == In 1973, the government launched _____, a conservation program aimed at protecting the national animal, the tiger",
      "answer": "Project Tiger",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India's initiatives such as green energy corridor and PM Surya ghar muft bijlii yojna promote renewable adoption.  The government allows 100% FDI in the sector and collaborates internationally (such as partnership with Australia) to boost investments.  Regardless of challenges like funding gap and skill shortages, India targets 500GW of renewable energy capacity by 2030.  == Environmentalism == In 1973, the government launched Project Tiger, a conservation program aimed at protecting the national animal, the tiger.  Its population reached as low as 2000 in 1970.  Human population growth, cultivation of forest land and mainly hunting were the key factors for this decline.  Aided by the World Wildlife Fund (WWF) and the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN), Indian conservationists were instrumental in getting the government to ban hunting and set aside national parks"
    },
