      "fact": " In 2024, the capital New Delhi recorded the country's hottest-ever temperature 49.  In response, New Delhi authorities warned citizens of water shortages, cutting supplies in some areas.  The water prime minister, Atishi Marlena, called for \"collective responsibility\" to deal with water scarcity and reduced water supply from twice a day to once a day in some areas.  Also in 2024, the heat waves caused problems for India's elections, when 33 poll workers died from extreme heat.  In India, exposure to heat waves is said to increase by 8 times between 2021 and 2050, and by 300% by the end of this century.  The number of Indians exposed to heat waves increased by 200% from 2010 to 2016.  Heat waves also affect farm labour productivity"
