      "subSubject": "Climate change in India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "=== International cooperation === As a party to the _____ submitted its first biennial transparency report to the UNFCCC by 2024 and inventory figures in standard format",
      "answer": "Paris Agreement India",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " As of 2020 the coal tax stands at ₹400 (US$4.  In contrast to implementing a carbon tax, in 2017, India spent US$1. 8 billion on fossil fuel subsidies, almost entirely on petroleum.  === International cooperation === As a party to the Paris Agreement India submitted its first biennial transparency report to the UNFCCC by 2024 and inventory figures in standard format.  In September 2021 India announced that it will submit a new Nationally Determined Contribution before COP26.  At COP26, India set the latest target date planning to be net-zero by 2070.  This was the first time in that a date for carbon neutrality has been given as part of India's climate policy"
    },
