      "answer": "1960",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Ghana is home to a growing indigenous Hindu population that today numbers 3000 families.  Hinduism first came to Ghana only in the late 1940s with the Sindhi traders who migrated here following India's Partition.  It has been growing in Ghana and neighbouring Togo since the mid-1970s when an African Hindu monastery was established in Accra.  Guinea Both countries established diplomatic relations on 8 July 1960.  Ivory Coast The bilateral relations between India and Ivory Coast have expanded considerably in recent years as India seeks to develop an extensive commercial and strategic partnership in the West African region.  The Indian diplomatic mission in Abidjan was opened in 1979.  Ivory Coast opened its resident mission in New Delhi in September 2004"
