      "fact": " After a period of tension, in 2017 Italian Prime Minister Paolo Gentiloni visited India and met his Indian counterpart Narendra Modi; they held extensive talks to strengthen the political cooperation and to boost the bilateral trade. There are around 150,000 people of Indian Origins living in Italy.  Around 1,000 Italian citizens reside in India, mostly working on behalf of Italian industrial groups.  Lithuania Luxembourg Relations were established in 1947, following India's independence.  Luxembourg operates an embassy in New Delhi whilst India operates a Consulate General in Luxembourg City.  Bilateral Trade stood at US$37 Million in 2014 and trade continues to grow every year.  Diplomats from both countries have visited the other several times"
