      "question": "India and Mauritius co-operate in combating piracy which has emerged as a major threat in the _____ region and support India's stand against terrorism",
      "answer": "Indian Ocean",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India has become Mauritius' largest source of imports since 2007 and Mauritius imported US$816 million worth of goods in the April 2010 – March 2011 financial year.  Mauritius has remained the largest source of FDI for India for more than a decade with FDI equity inflows totalling US$55. 2 billion in the period April 2000 to April 2011.  India and Mauritius co-operate in combating piracy which has emerged as a major threat in the Indian Ocean region and support India's stand against terrorism.  The relationship between Mauritius and India date back to the early 1730s, when artisans were brought from Puducherry and Tamil Nadu.  Diplomatic relations between India and Mauritius were established in 1948.  Mauritius maintained contacts with India through successive Dutch, French and British rule"
