      "fact": " India receives 40,000 barrels per day (6,400 m3/d) from Nigeria.  Trade between these two countries stands at $875 million in 2005–2006.  Indian companies have also invested in manufacturing, pharmaceuticals, iron ore, steel, information technology, and communications, amongst other things.  Both India and Nigeria, are members of the Commonwealth of Nations, G-77, and the Non-Aligned Movement.  Former Nigerian president, Olusegun Obasanjo was the guest of honour, at the Republic Day parade, in 1999, and the Indian prime minister Manmohan Singh visited Nigeria in 2007 and addressed the Nigerian Parliament.  Rwanda Indo-Rwandan relations are the foreign relations between the Republic of India and the Republic of Rwanda.  India is represented in Rwanda through its honorary consulate in Kigali"
    },
