      "fact": " Since the mid-1980s when President Yoweri Museveni came to power, relations have steadily improved.  Today some 20,000 Indians and PIOs live or work in Uganda.  Ethnic tensions between Indians and Ugandans have been a recurring issue in bilateral relations given the role of Indians in the Ugandan economy.  Zambia Zimbabwe African Union As of the year 2011, India's total trade with Africa is over US$46 billion and its total investment is over US$11 billion with a US$5. 7 billion line of credit for executing various projects in Africa.  India has had good relationships with most sub-Saharan African nations for most of its history.  In the Prime Minister's visit to Mauritius in 1997, the two countries secured a deal to new Credit Agreement of INR 105 million (US$3 million) to finance the import by Mauritius of capital goods, consultancy services and consumer durable from India"
