      "emoji": "",
      "question": "India is represented in Paraguay through its embassy in _____ in Argentina",
      "answer": "Buenos Aires",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In seeking to rapidly strengthen trade relations such as the flow of trade triples between the two countries, India is keen to leverage these transit trade facilities in Panama to access the wider market of Latin America.  Along with pursuing a free trade agreement, India wants to promote investment in various sectors of Panama's economy, including the banking and maritime industry and the multimodal centre of the Colón Free Trade Zone.  Paraguay The bilateral relations between the Republic of India and Paraguay have been traditionally strong due to strong commercial, cultural and strategic cooperation.  India is represented in Paraguay through its embassy in Buenos Aires in Argentina.  India also has an Honorary Consul-General in Asuncion.  Paraguay opened its embassy in India in 2005.  In May 2012, Fernando Lugo became the first Paraguayan President to visit India"
    },
