      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:30:19.019Z",
      "subject": "International Relations",
      "subSubject": "Foreign relations of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "_____ 2012, Fernando Lugo became the first Paraguayan President to visit India",
      "answer": "In May",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India is represented in Paraguay through its embassy in Buenos Aires in Argentina.  India also has an Honorary Consul-General in Asuncion.  Paraguay opened its embassy in India in 2005.  In May 2012, Fernando Lugo became the first Paraguayan President to visit India.  He was accompanied by the Ministers of Foreign Affairs, Agriculture and Animal Husbandry and Commerce, and other senior government officials.  Paraguay supported India's bid for election to the UN Human Rights Council for the term 2015–17.  On 30 December 2020, the Union Cabinet of India approved the opening an embassy in Asunción"
