      "subSubject": "Foreign relations of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "This has been praised by the Argentine media, public and the _____ himself",
      "answer": "Foreign Minister",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Under the new visa agreement signed during the Argentine Presidential visit in October 2009, it has been agreed that five-year multi-entry business visas would be given free of cost.  The Embassy of India in Buenos Aires gives Cafe Con Visa (coffee with visa) to Argentine visitors.  The applicants are invited for coffee and a visa is given immediately.  This has been praised by the Argentine media, public and the Foreign Minister himself. \" Brazil Relations between Brazil and India have been extended to diverse areas such as science and technology, pharmaceuticals and space as both are member nations of BRICS.  The two-way trade in 2007 nearly tripled to US$3.  India attaches tremendous importance to its relationship with this Latin American giant and hopes to see the areas of cooperation expand in the coming years"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2912",
