      "subSubject": "Foreign relations of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "India also signed four other pacts, including an extradition treaty, in the presence of _____ and her Kazakh counterpart Nursultan Nazarbayev",
      "answer": "President Prathibha Patil",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The two countries are collaborating in petrochemicals, information technology, and space technology.  Kazakhstan has offered India five blocks for oil and gas exploration.  India and Kazakhstan, are to set up joint projects in construction, minerals and metallurgy.  India also signed four other pacts, including an extradition treaty, in the presence of President Prathibha Patil and her Kazakh counterpart Nursultan Nazarbayev.  Kazakhstan will provide Uranium and related products under the MoU between Nuclear Power Corp.  of India and Kazatomprom.  These MoU also open possibilities of joint exploration of uranium in Kazakhstan, which has the world's second-largest reserves, and India building atomic power plants in the Central Asian country"
    },
