      "question": "_____ and North Korea have growing trade and diplomatic relations",
      "answer": "North Korea India",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India established diplomatic relations in December 1955.  India was the first country outside the Soviet bloc to establish diplomatic relations with Mongolia.  Since then, there have been treaties of mutual friendship and cooperation between the two countries in 1973, 1994, 2001 and 2004.  North Korea India and North Korea have growing trade and diplomatic relations.  India had a fully functioning embassy in Pyongyang which was closed down due to COVID-19 pandemic in the host country while North Korea still operates an embassy in New Delhi.  India has said that it wants the \"reunification\" of Korea.  South Korea The cordial relationship between the two countries extends back to 48AD, when Queen Suro, or Princess Heo, travelled from the kingdom of Ayodhya to Korea"
    },
    {
      "id": "q2942",
      "type": "fill_blank",
