      "question": "To connect Kolkata with Tripura via Bangladesh through railway, the _____ on 10 February 2016 sanctioned about 580 crore rupees",
      "answer": "Union Government",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India and Bangladesh also have free trade agreement on 7 June 2015.  Both countries solved their border dispute on 6 June 2015.  The Agartala-Akhaura rail link between Indian Railway and Bangladesh Railway will reduce the current 1700 km road distance between Kolkata to Agartala via Siliguri to just 350 kilometre by railway.  To connect Kolkata with Tripura via Bangladesh through railway, the Union Government on 10 February 2016 sanctioned about 580 crore rupees.  The project which is expected to be completed by 2017 will pass through Bangladesh.  The project ranks high on Prime Minister's 'Act East Policy', and is expected to increase connectivity and boost trade between India and Bangladesh.  Bhutan Historically, there have been close ties with India"
    },
