      "answer": "Georgian Ministry",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India has consistently supported and voted for a peaceful resolution of the Cyprus dispute at the United Nations.  Georgia Georgia has an embassy in New Delhi.  India is represented in Georgia through its embassy in Yerevan (Armenia) and an honorary consulate in Tbilisi.  Georgian Ministry of Foreign Affairs about relations with India Iran Independent India and Iran established diplomatic links on 15 March 1950.  After the Iranian Revolution of 1979, Iran withdrew from CENTO and dissociated itself from US-friendly countries, including Pakistan, which automatically meant an improved relationship with the Republic of India.  Currently, the two countries have friendly relations in many areas.  There are significant trade ties, particularly in crude oil imports into India and diesel exports to Iran"
    },
