      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India's strategic relations with Saudi Arabia have been affected by the latter's close ties with Pakistan.  Saudi Arabia supported Pakistan's stance on the Kashmir conflict during the Indo-Pakistani War of 1971 at the expense of its relations with India.  The Soviet Union's close relations with India also served as a source of consternation.  During the Persian Gulf War (1990–91), India officially maintained neutrality.  Saudi Arabia's close military and strategic ties with Pakistan have also been a source of continuing strain.  Since the 1990s, both nations have taken steps to improve ties.  Saudi Arabia has supported granting observer status to India in the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation (OIC) and has expanded its cooperation with India to fight terrorism"
