      "question": "_____ has an embassy in New Delhi, and India has an embassy in Copenhagen",
      "answer": "Denmark Denmark",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Czech Republic has an embassy in New Delhi.  Consulates of the Czech Republic in India are in Chennai, Mumbai and Kolkata.  India has an embassy in Prague.  Denmark Denmark has an embassy in New Delhi, and India has an embassy in Copenhagen.  Tranquebar, a town in the southern Indian state of Tamil Nadu, was a Danish colony in India from 1620 to 1845.  It is spelled Trankebar or Tranquebar in Danish, which comes from the native Tamil, Tarangambadi, meaning \"place of the singing waves\".  It was sold, along with the other Danish settlements in mainland India, most notably Serampore (now in West Bengal), to Great Britain in 1845"
    },
    {
