      "fact": " It gives detailed information about the ports, routes and commodities.  The Greek ethnographer and explorer of the Hellenistic period, Megasthenes was the ambassador of Seleucus I in India.  In his work, Indika (Greek: Ινδικά), he wrote the history of Indians and their culture.  Megasthenes also mentioned the prehistoric arrival of the God Dionysus and Herakles (Megasthenes' Herakles) in India.  There is now tangible evidence indicating that the settlement of Greek merchants in Bengal must have begun as early as the beginning of the seventeenth century.  Dimitrios Galanos (Greek: Δημήτριος Γαλανός, 1760–1833) was the earliest recorded Greek Indologist.  His translations of Sanskrit texts into Greek made knowledge of the philosophical and religious ideas of India available to many Europeans"
