      "answer": "An Apostolic Delegation",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " India is the second largest investor in Britain after the US.  Britain is also one of the largest investors in India.  Vatican City & the Holy See Formal bilateral relations between India and Vatican City have existed since 12 June 1948.  An Apostolic Delegation existed in India from 1881.  The Holy See has a nunciature in New Delhi whilst India has accredited its embassy in Bern, Switzerland to the Holy See as well.  India's Ambassador in Bern has traditionally been accredited to the Holy See.  The connections between the Catholic Church and India can be traced back to the apostle St"
    },
