      "fact": " == De Facto == Kosovo Since its declaration of independence from Serbia, Kosovo sought recognition from the major of the world's most influential countries, among them, India.  Indian views regarding the developments followed initial constringent to comment but dismissed to give recognition of statehood.  There are almost negligible interactions.  Palestine After India achieved its independence in 1947, the country moved to support Palestinian self-determination following the partition of India.  In light of a religious partition between India and Pakistan, the impetus to boost ties with Muslim states around the world was a further tie to India's support for the Palestinian cause.  Though it started to waver in the late 1980s and 1990s, as the recognition of Israel led to diplomatic exchanges, the ultimate support for the Palestinian cause, was still an underlying concern.  Beyond the recognition of Palestinian self-determination ties have been largely dependent upon socio-cultural bonds, while economic relations were neither cold nor warm"
