      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The court can also be called upon by other UN organs to provide advisory opinions on matters of international law.  All UN member states are parties to the ICJ Statute, which forms an integral part of the UN Charter, and non-members may also become parties.  The ICJ's rulings are binding upon parties and, along with its advisory opinions, serve as sources of international law.  The court is composed of 15 judges appointed to nine-year terms by the General Assembly.  Every sitting judge must be from a different nation.  === Economic and Social Council === The Economic and Social Council (ECOSOC) assists the General Assembly in promoting international economic and social co-operation and development.  It was established to serve as the UN's primary forum for global issues and is the largest and most complex UN body"
