      "answer": "Social Council",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The ICJ's rulings are binding upon parties and, along with its advisory opinions, serve as sources of international law.  The court is composed of 15 judges appointed to nine-year terms by the General Assembly.  Every sitting judge must be from a different nation.  === Economic and Social Council === The Economic and Social Council (ECOSOC) assists the General Assembly in promoting international economic and social co-operation and development.  It was established to serve as the UN's primary forum for global issues and is the largest and most complex UN body.  The ECOSOC's functions include gathering data, conducting studies and advising and making recommendations to member states.  Its work is carried out primarily by subsidiary bodies focused on a wide variety of topics"
