      "fact": " High Courts that handle large numbers of cases have permanent benches (or a branch of the court).  For litigants of remote regions, 'circuit benches' work on those days when judges visit.  === District Courts === The District Courts of India are established by state governments for every district or group of districts, taking into account the number of cases and population distribution.  These courts are under administrative control of the state's High Court.  Decisions are subject to the appeal to the High Court.  The District Court is presided over by one District Judge appointed by the Governor with the consultation of High Court.  Additional District Judges and Assistant District Judges may be appointee depending on the workload"
