      "question": "The spacecraft carries the _____ in X-rays (POLIX) payload which will study the degree and angle of polarisation of bright astronomical X-ray sources in the energy range 5–30 keV",
      "answer": "Polarimeter Instrument",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " === Astrosat === Launched in 2015, Astrosat is India's first dedicated multi-wavelength space observatory.  Its observation study includes active galactic nuclei, hot White dwarfs, pulsations of pulsars, binary star systems, and supermassive black holes located at the centre of the galaxy.  === XPoSat === The X-ray Polarimeter Satellite (XPoSat) is a satellite for studying black holes and polarisation.  The spacecraft carries the Polarimeter Instrument in X-rays (POLIX) payload which will study the degree and angle of polarisation of bright astronomical X-ray sources in the energy range 5–30 keV.  It launched on 1 January 2024 on a PSLV-DL rocket, and it has an expected operational lifespan of at least five years.  == Extraterrestrial exploration == === Lunar exploration === Chandryaan (lit.  'Mooncraft') are India's series of lunar exploration spacecraft"
    },
