      "answer": "Kumar Shri Duleepsinhji",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " As part of 14 consecutive victories in the Ranji Trophy from 1958–59 to 1972–73, Bombay won the title in all ten seasons of the period under review.  Among its players were Farokh Engineer, Dilip Sardesai, Bapu Nadkarni, Ramakant Desai, Baloo Gupte, Ashok Mankad and Ajit Wadekar.  The Duleep Trophy was inaugurated as a zonal competition in the 1961–1962 season.  It was named after Ranji's nephew, Kumar Shri Duleepsinhji (1905–59).  With Bombay in its catchment, it is not surprising that the West Zone won six of the first nine titles.  === 1970 to 1985 === Bombay ( now Mumbai) continued to dominate Indian domestic cricket, with only Karnataka, Delhi, and a few other teams able to mount any kind of challenge during this period.  India enjoyed two international highlights"
