      "answer": "Irani Trophy",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The original format had five teams, which were drawn from the five zones (i.  North, South, East, West and central) and played each other on a knock-out basis.  From the 1993–94 season, the competition has been converted to a league format.  Irani Trophy – The Irani Trophy tournament was conceived during the 1959–60 season to mark the completion of 25 years of the Ranji Trophy championship and was named after the late Z.  Irani, who was associated with the Board of Control for Cricket in India (BCCI) from its inception in 1928, till his death in 1970 and a keen patron of the game.  The first match, played between the Ranji Trophy champions and the Rest of India was played in 1959–60.  For the first few years, it was played at the tail end of the season"
