      "question": "==== 2020 ==== In 2019, the _____ of Education released a draft of a new education policy, which was followed by a number of public consultations",
      "answer": "Indian Ministry",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The Nehru government sponsored the development of high-quality scientific education institutions such as the Indian Institutes of Technology.  In 1961, the Union government formed the National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) as an autonomous organisation that would advise both the Union and state governments on formulating and implementing education policies.  In 2015, the Swach Vidyalaya had finished which was an initiative to put a functional toilet in every school.  ==== 2020 ==== In 2019, the Indian Ministry of Education released a draft of a new education policy, which was followed by a number of public consultations.  It discusses reducing curriculum content to enhance essential learning, critical thinking, and promoting more holistic, experiential, discussion-based and analysis-based learning.  It also talks about a revision of the curriculum and pedagogical structure from a 10+2 system to a 5+3+3+4 system design in an effort to optimise learning for students based on cognitive development of children.  On 29 July 2020, the cabinet approved a new National Education Policy with an aim to introduce several changes to the existing Indian education system"
    },
