      "question": "Preschool for _____ states that almost 99% of pre-schools do not have any curriculum at all",
      "answer": "Child Rights",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "5% of the schools had a playground.  === Curriculum issues === Modern education in India is often criticised for being based on rote learning rather than problem solving.  Rajvanshi writes that the Indian education system seems to be producing zombies since in most of the schools students seemed to be spending majority of their time in preparing for competitive exams rather than learning or playing.  Preschool for Child Rights states that almost 99% of pre-schools do not have any curriculum at all.  Also, creativity is not encouraged and is considered a form of entertainment in most institutions.  The 2009 Hindi movie 3 Idiots specifically highlighted these issues, which led to major debates, especially in higher education.  The British \"essentialist\" view of knowledge of the nineteenth century emphasised the individual, scientific, universal, and moral aims of education ahead of the social and cultural"
    },
