      "fact": " a reservation of 15% in Kendriya Vidyalaya for Scheduled Castes and another reservation of 7. 5% in Kendriya Vidyalaya for Scheduled Tribes.  Similar reservations are held by the Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes in many schemes and educational facilities in India.  The remote and far-flung regions of North-East India are provided for under the Non-Lapsible Central pool of Resources (NLCPR) since 1998–1999.  The NLCPR aims to provide funds for infrastructure development in these remote areas.  Women from remote, underdeveloped areas or from weaker social groups in Andhra Pradesh, Assam, Bihar, Jharkhand, Karnataka, Kerala, Gujarat, Uttar Pradesh, and Uttarakhand, fall under the Mahila Samakhya Scheme, initiated in 1989.  Apart from provisions for education this programme also aims to raise awareness by holding meetings and seminars at rural levels"
