      "question": "_____ was renamed Karnataka in 1973",
      "answer": "Mysore State",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The act designated Chandigarh as a union territory and the shared capital of Punjab and Haryana.  Madras State was renamed Tamil Nadu in 1969.  The north-eastern states of Manipur, Meghalaya and Tripura were formed on 21 January 1972.  Mysore State was renamed Karnataka in 1973.  On 16 May 1975, Sikkim became the 22nd state of the Indian Union and the state's monarchy was abolished.  In 1987, Arunachal Pradesh and Mizoram became states on 20 February, followed by Goa on 30 May, while erstwhile union territory of Goa, Daman and Diu's northern exclaves Damão and Diu became a separate union territory as Daman and Diu.  In November 2000, three new states were created, namely: Chhattisgarh, from eastern Madhya Pradesh, (Madhya Pradesh Reorganisation Act, 2000) Uttaranchal, from northwest Uttar Pradesh (renamed Uttarakhand in 2007), (Uttar Pradesh Reorganisation Act, 2000), and Jharkhand, from southern districts of Bihar (Bihar Reorganisation Act, 2000)"
