      "id": "q4135",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "State GK",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:32:14.675Z",
      "subject": "State GK",
      "subSubject": "Maharashtra",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "After the partial autonomy given to the states by the Government of _____ 1935, B",
      "answer": "India Act",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The modern struggle for independence started taking shape in the late 1800s with leaders such as Bal Gangadhar Tilak, Justice Mahadev Govind Ranade, Gopal Krishna Gokhale, Pherozeshah Mehta and Dadabhai Naoroji evaluating the company rule and its consequences.  Jyotirao Phule was the pioneer of social reform in the Maharashtra region in the second half of the 19th century.  Shahu, Raja of Kolhapur and continued Phule's work, as well as B.  After the partial autonomy given to the states by the Government of India Act 1935, B.  Kher became the first chief minister of the Congress party-led government of the trilingual Bombay Presidency.  The ultimatum to the British during the Quit India Movement was given in Mumbai and culminated in the transfer of power and independence in 1947.  After Indian independence, princely states and Jagirs of the Deccan States Agency were merged into Bombay State, which was created from the former Bombay Presidency in 1950"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4136",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "State GK",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:32:14.675Z",
      "subject": "State GK",
      "subSubject": "Maharashtra",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "Kher became the first chief minister of the Congress party-led government of the trilingual _____",
      "answer": "Bombay Presidency",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Jyotirao Phule was the pioneer of social reform in the Maharashtra region in the second half of the 19th century.  Shahu, Raja of Kolhapur and continued Phule's work, as well as B.  After the partial autonomy given to the states by the Government of India Act 1935, B.  Kher became the first chief minister of the Congress party-led government of the trilingual Bombay Presidency.  The ultimatum to the British during the Quit India Movement was given in Mumbai and culminated in the transfer of power and independence in 1947.  After Indian independence, princely states and Jagirs of the Deccan States Agency were merged into Bombay State, which was created from the former Bombay Presidency in 1950.  In 1956, the States Reorganisation Act reorganised the Indian states along linguistic lines, and Bombay Presidency State was enlarged by the addition of the predominantly Marathi-speaking regions of Marathwada (Aurangabad Division) from erstwhile Hyderabad state and Vidarbha region from the Central Provinces and Berar"
    },
