      "question": "Nashik, _____, Dhule and Bhusawal are the major cities of this region",
      "answer": "Malegaon Jalgaon",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Maharashtra is divided into five geographic regions.  Konkan is the western coastal region, between the Western Ghats and the sea.  Khandesh is the north region lying in the valley of the Tapti, Purna river.  Nashik, Malegaon Jalgaon, Dhule and Bhusawal are the major cities of this region.  Desh is in the centre of the state.  Marathwada, which was a part of the princely state of Hyderabad until 1956, is located in the southeastern part of the state.  Aurangabad and Nanded are the main cities of the region"
    },
