      "fact": " Due to this the agricultural productivity of Maharashtra is generally low as compared to the national averages of various crops.  Maharashtra has been divided in to nine agro-climatic zones on the basis of annual rainfall soil types, vegetation and cropping pattern.  === Climate === Maharashtra experiences a tropical wet and dry climate with hot, rainy, and cold weather seasons.  Some areas more inland experience a hot semi arid climate, due to a rain shadow effect caused by the Western Ghats.  The month of March marks the beginning of the summer and the temperature rises steadily until June.  In the central plains, summer temperatures rise to between 40 °C or 104. 0 °F and 45 °C or 113"
