      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The 2011 census found scheduled castes and scheduled tribes to account for 11. 9% of the population, respectively.  The state also includes a substantial number of migrants from other states of India.  Uttar Pradesh, Gujarat, and Karnataka account for the largest percentage of migrants to the Mumbai metropolitan area.  The 2011 census reported the human sex ratio is 929 females per 1000 males, which were below the national average of 943.  The density of Maharashtra was 365 inhabitants per km2 which was lower than the national average of 382 per km2.  Since 1921, the populations of Ratnagiri and Sindhudurg shrank by −4"
