      "question": "_____, a wide range of languages are spoken, including Gujarati, Telugu, Tamil, Konkani, Kannada, Sindhi, Punjabi, Bengali, Tulu, and many more",
      "answer": "In Mumbai",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Combined with Urdu, the persianized register of Hindustani, speakers of Hindi-Urdu form nearly 20% of the Maharashtrian population.  Urdu and another Hindustani dialect, Dakhni, are spoken primarily by the Muslim population of the state.  The Mumbai metropolitan area is home to migrants from all over India.  In Mumbai, a wide range of languages are spoken, including Gujarati, Telugu, Tamil, Konkani, Kannada, Sindhi, Punjabi, Bengali, Tulu, and many more.  == Governance and administration == The state is governed through a parliamentary system of representative democracy, a feature the state shares with other Indian states.  Maharashtra is one of the six states in India where the state legislature is bicameral, comprising the Vidhan Sabha (Legislative Assembly) and the Vidhan Parishad (Legislative Council).  The legislature, the Maharashtra Legislative Assembly, consists of elected members and special office bearers such as the Speaker and Deputy Speaker, who are elected by the members"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4163",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "State GK",
      "region": "",
