      "answer": "Traditional Malvani",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Varan is nothing but plain dal, a common Indian lentil stew.  More or less, most of the dishes use coconut, onion, garlic, ginger, red chili powder, green chilies, and mustard though some section of the population traditionally avoid onion and garlics.  Maharashtrian cuisine varies with the regions.  Traditional Malvani (Konkani), Kolhapuri, and Varhadhi dishes are examples of well known regional cuisines.  Kolhapur is famous for Tambda Pandhra rassa, a dish made of either chicken or mutton.  Rice and seafood are the staple foods of the coastal Konkani people.  Among seafood, the most popular is a fish variety called the Bombay duck (also known as bombil in Marathi)"
