      "hint": "",
      "fact": " While dancing, they are divided into groups of two.  These fishermen display the movements of waves and casting of the nets during their koli dance performances.  === Theatre === Modern Theatre in Maharashtra can trace its origins to the British colonial era in the middle of the 19th century.  It is modelled mainly after the western tradition but also includes forms like Sangeet Natak (musical drama).  In recent decades, Marathi Tamasha has also been incorporated in some experimental plays.  The repertoire of Marathi theatre ranges from humorous social plays, farces, historical plays, and musical, to experimental plays and serious drama.  Marathi Playwrights such as Vijay Tendulkar, Purushottam Laxman Deshpande, Mahesh Elkunchwar, Ratnakar Matkari, and Satish Alekar have influenced theatre throughout India"
