      "answer": "Sachin Pilgaonkar",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In earliest days of Marathi cinema, Suryakant Mandhare was a leading star.  In later years, Shriram Lagoo, Nilu Phule, Vikram Gokhale, Dilip Prabhavalkar played character roles in theatre, and Hindi and Marathi films.  Ramesh Deo and Mohan Joshi played leading men in Mainstream Marathi movies.  In 70s and 80s, Sachin Pilgaonkar, Ashok Saraf, Laxmikant Berde and Mahesh Kothare created a \"comedy film wave\" in Marathi Cinema.  == Media == The state is home to more than 200 newspapers and 350 consumer magazines.  The publishing industry employs more than 250,000 people.  There are number of Marathi news channels in the state viz News18 Lokmat, ABP Majha"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4247",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "State GK",
