      "fact": " All India Radio airs its content through multiple channels including Air Marathi, FM Gold, and FM Rainbow.  Air India's commercially successful air channel Vividh Bharti is headquartered in Mumbai.  Private radio stations like Big 92. 7 FM, Radio Mirchi, Red FM, Vasundhara Vahini, Radio Dhamaal 24, and My FM air in all major cities.  Airtel, BSNL, Jio, and VI networks provide cellular services and have covered most of the Maharashtra.  Broadband internet is available in most of the towns, villages, and cities, provided by the state-run MTNL and BSNL and by other private companies.  == Sports == Cricket is the most popular spectator sport in Maharashtra"
