      "answer": "1749",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " George, the first major English settlement in India, which became the nucleus of the British Raj in the region.  By 1693, the French established trading posts at Pondichéry.  In September 1746, the French captured Madras during the Battle of Madras.  The British regained control of Madras in 1749 through the Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle and resisted a French siege attempt in 1759.  The British and French competed to expand the trade which led to Battle of Wandiwash in 1760 as part of the Seven Years' War.  The Nawabs of the Carnatic surrendered much of their territory to the British East India Company in the north and bestowed tax revenue collection rights in the South, which led to constant conflicts with the Palaiyakkarars known as the Polygar Wars.  Puli Thevar was one of the earliest opponents, joined later by Rani Velu Nachiyar of Sivagangai and Kattabomman of Panchalakurichi in the first series of Polygar wars"
    },
