      "question": "The Greater Chennai Corporation, established in _____, is the second oldest in the world and Tamil Nadu was the first state to establish town panchayats as a new administrative uni",
      "answer": "1688",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The taluks are divided into 1349 revenue blocks called Firkas which consist of 17,680 revenue villages.  The local administration consists of a single tier system for urban areas, which are governed by either of the three types of urban bodies–municipal corporation, municipality, or town panchayat, based on revenue and population.  As of 2026, there are 25 municipal corporations, 138 municipalities and 528 town panchayats in the state.  The Greater Chennai Corporation, established in 1688, is the second oldest in the world and Tamil Nadu was the first state to establish town panchayats as a new administrative unit.  The rural administration consists of a three-tier Panchayati Raj system with the district panchayats at the district level, panchayat unions at the intermediate (block) level, and village panchayats at the village level.  As of 2026, there are 36 district panchayats, 288 panchayat unions and 12,525 village panchayats, administered by village administrative officers.  === Legislature === In accordance with the Constitution of India, the governor is a state's de jure head and appoints the chief minister who has the de facto executive authority"
    },
