      "emoji": "",
      "question": "_____ is a type of cotton sari made in the Coimbatore",
      "answer": "Kovai Cora",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Women wear colourful silk saris on special occasions such as marriages.  The Kanchipuram silk sari is a type of silk sari made in the Kanchipuram region in Tamil Nadu and these saris are worn as a part of the bridal attire and during special occasions.  It has been recognised as a Geographical indication by the Government of India in 2005–2006.  Kovai Cora is a type of cotton sari made in the Coimbatore.  Young girls wear a long skirt called pavaadai along with a long over cloth called dhavani.  The men wear a veshti, a rectangular piece of non-stitched cloth, of varying lengths, that is wrapped around the legs and knotted at the waist.  It is often white, bordered in brightly coloured stripes"
    },
