      "answer": "Chennai Metro",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The state has 116 large dams.  Apart from the rivers, the majority of the water comes from rainwater stored in more than 41,000 tanks and 1. 68 million wells across the state.  Water supply and sewage treatment are managed by the respective local administrative bodies such as the Chennai MetroWater Supply and Sewage Board in Chennai.  Desalination plants including the country's largest at Minjur provide alternative means of drinking water.  As per the 2011 census, only 83. 4% of the households have access to safe drinking water, less than the national average of 85"
