      "fact": " Traditional martial arts include Silambattam, Gatta gusthi, and Adimurai.  Cricket is the most popular sport in the state.  Chidambaram Stadium established in 1916 is among the oldest cricket stadiums in India and has hosted matches during multiple ICC Cricket World Cups.  Established in 1987, MRF Pace Foundation is a bowling academy based in Chennai.  Chennai is home to the most successful Indian Premier League (IPL) cricket team, Chennai Super Kings, and hosted the finals during the 2011, 2012, and 2024 seasons.  Football is also popular with the Indian Super League being the major club competition and Chennaiyin FC representing the state.  There are multi-purpose venues in major cities including Chennai and Coimbatore, which host football and athletics"
