      "question": "Coimbatore is often referred to as \"India's _____\" and the \"Backyard of Indian Motorsports\" and hosts the Kari Motor Speedway, a Formula 3 Category circuit",
      "answer": "Motorsports Hub",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " A large number of automotive companies have their manufacturing bases in the state with the automotive industry in Chennai accounting for more than 35% of India's overall automotive components and automobile output, earning the nickname \"Detroit of India\".  The Integral Coach Factory in Chennai manufactures railway coaches and other rolling stock for Indian Railways.  Another major industry is textiles with the state being home to more than half of the operating fiber textile mills in India.  Coimbatore is often referred to as the Manchester of South India due to its cotton production and textile industries.  As of 2022, Tiruppur exported garments worth US$480 billion, contributing to nearly 54% of the all the textile exports from India and the city is known as the knitwear capital due to its cotton knitwear export.  As of 2015, the textile industry in Tamil Nadu accounts for 17% of the total invested capital in all the industries.  As of 2021, 40% of leather goods exported from India worth ₹92"
    },
