      "answer": "Yashodhara Charitha",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Other famous poets like Ponna wrote \"shantinatapurana\", \"Bhuvanaikaramabhyudaya\", \"Jinaksharamale\", and \"gatapratyagata\".  Ranna wrote \"Shantipurana\" and \"Ghadayudha\".  The Jain poet Nagavarma II wrote \"Kavyavalokana\", \"Karnatabhashabhushana\" and \"Vardhamanapurana\" .  Janna was the author of \"Yashodhara Charitha\".  Rudhrabhatta and Durgashima wrote \"Jagannatha Vijaya\" and \"Panchatantra\" respectively.  The works of the medieval period are based on Jain and Hindu principles.  The Vachana Sahitya tradition of the 12th century is purely native and unique in world literature"
