      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Andrews, Irish poet William Butler Yeats, Ezra Pound, Robert Bridges, Ernest Rhys, Thomas Sturge Moore, and others.  Yeats wrote the preface to the English translation of Gitanjali; Andrews joined Tagore at Santiniketan.  In November 1912 Tagore began touring the United States and the United Kingdom, staying in Butterton, Staffordshire with Andrews's clergymen friends.  From May 1916 until April 1917, he lectured in Japan and the United States.  He denounced nationalism.  His essay \"Nationalism in India\" was scorned and praised; it was admired by Romain Rolland and other pacifists.  Shortly after returning home, the 63-year-old Tagore accepted an invitation from the Peruvian government"
    },
