      "question": "His essay \"Nationalism in India\" was scorned and praised; it was admired by _____ and other pacifists",
      "answer": "Romain Rolland",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In November 1912 Tagore began touring the United States and the United Kingdom, staying in Butterton, Staffordshire with Andrews's clergymen friends.  From May 1916 until April 1917, he lectured in Japan and the United States.  He denounced nationalism.  His essay \"Nationalism in India\" was scorned and praised; it was admired by Romain Rolland and other pacifists.  Shortly after returning home, the 63-year-old Tagore accepted an invitation from the Peruvian government.  He travelled to Mexico.  Each government pledged US$100,000 to his school to commemorate the visits"
    },
