      "question": "Visits to Persia and Iraq (in 1932) and _____ (in 1933) composed Tagore's final foreign tour, and his dislike of communalism and nationalism only deepened",
      "answer": "Sri Lanka",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In April 1932 Tagore, intrigued by the Persian mystic Hafez, was hosted by Reza Shah Pahlavi.  In his other travels, Tagore interacted with Henri Bergson, Albert Einstein, Robert Frost, Thomas Mann, George Bernard Shaw, H.  Wells, and Romain Rolland.  Visits to Persia and Iraq (in 1932) and Sri Lanka (in 1933) composed Tagore's final foreign tour, and his dislike of communalism and nationalism only deepened.  Vice-president of India M.  Hamid Ansari has said that Rabindranath Tagore heralded the cultural rapprochement between communities, societies and nations much before it became the liberal norm of conduct.  Tagore was a man ahead of his time"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4531",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Books & Authors",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:32:26.517Z",
