      "fact": " As of February 2026, the award has been conferred upon 53 people with 18 posthumous declarations.  == Regulations == The Bharat Ratna is conferred \"in recognition of exceptional service/performance of the highest order\", without distinction of race, occupation, position, or gender.  The award was originally confined to the arts, literature, science, and public services, as per the 1954 regulations.  In December 2011, the rules were amended to \"any field of human endeavour\".  The 1954 statutes did not allow posthumous awards, but this was subsequently modified in the January 1966 statute, and Lal Bahadur Shastri became the first recipient to be honored posthumously in 1966.  Although there is no formal nomination process, recommendations for the award can only be made by the prime minister to the president.  The recipient receives a Sanad (certificate) signed by the president and a medallion without any monetary grant"
