      "question": "Centre also recognises innovative startups and ecosystem contributors through annual _____ ceremoney",
      "answer": "National Startup Awards",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The initiative also exempts startups from income tax for three consecutive years and benefits from capital gains tax relief.  The Credit Guarantee Scheme provides a collateral-free loan up to ₹5 crore through the National Credit Guarantee Trust Company.  === Incubation and industry partnerships === As of 2024, 68 centres have been established in academic and research institutions under Startup India initiative known as Atal Incubation Centres (AICs).  Centre also recognises innovative startups and ecosystem contributors through annual National Startup Awards ceremoney.  The initiative has implemented startup policies in 30 states and union territories aligning with the central framework.  == Eligibility criteria == To be recognised under Startup India, an enterprise must fulfil the required conditions.  It should: Be a private limited company, registered partnership firm, or limited liability partnership"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4795",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "Business & Economy",
      "region": "",
