      "question": "On 29 February 1964 and 1968, he became the only _____ to present the Union Budget on his birthday",
      "answer": "Finance Minister",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The total expenditure was estimated at ₹197. 29 crore, with Defence expenditure constituting ₹92.  The Union Budgets for the fiscal years 1959–61 to 1963–64, including the interim budget for 1962–63, were presented by Morarji Desai.  On 29 February 1964 and 1968, he became the only Finance Minister to present the Union Budget on his birthday.  Desai presented a total of five annual budgets and an interim budget during his first term, and three final budgets and one interim budget during his second term, when he served as both the Finance Minister and the Deputy Prime Minister of India.  After Desai's resignation, Indira Gandhi, the then Prime Minister, took over the Ministry of Finance, becoming the first woman to hold the post of Finance Minister in India.  Patel presented the shortest budget speech for the interim budget of 1977, which was merely 800 words long"
    },
