      "question": "=== _____–1949 === The Reserve Bank of India was founded on 1 April 1935 to respond to economic troubles after the First World War",
      "answer": "1935",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " His economic principles continue to influence India's financial policies and central banking regulations.  The Reserve Bank of India was established in 1934, under the Reserve Bank of India Act.  Though privately owned initially, it was nationalised in 1949 and since then fully owned by the Ministry of Finance, Government of India (GoI).  === 1935–1949 === The Reserve Bank of India was founded on 1 April 1935 to respond to economic troubles after the First World War.  The bank was set up based on the recommendations of the 1926 Royal Commission on Indian Currency and Finance, also known as the Hilton Young Commission.  Eventually, the Central Legislative Assembly passed these guidelines as the RBI Act 1934.  India was the first colony to have its own central bank"
    },
