      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:34:40.588Z",
      "subject": "RBI Press Releases",
      "subSubject": "Reserve Bank of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "Two payment systems _____ (NEFT) and Real-Time Gross Settlement (RTGS) allow individuals, companies and firms to transfer funds from one bank to another",
      "answer": "National Electronic Fund Transfer",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " === Regulator and supervisor of the payment and settlement systems === Payment and settlement systems play an important role in improving overall economic efficiency.  The Payment and Settlement Systems Act of 2007 (PSS Act) gives the Reserve Bank oversight authority, including regulation and supervision, for the payment and settlement systems in the country.  In this role, the RBI focuses on the development and functioning of safe, secure and efficient payment and settlement mechanisms.  Two payment systems National Electronic Fund Transfer (NEFT) and Real-Time Gross Settlement (RTGS) allow individuals, companies and firms to transfer funds from one bank to another.  These facilities can only be used for transferring money within the country.  From 16-December-2019, one can transfer money online using the National Electronic Funds Transfer (NEFT) route 24x7, i. , any time of the day and any day of the week"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4967",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "RBI Press Releases",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:34:40.588Z",
      "subject": "RBI Press Releases",
      "subSubject": "Reserve Bank of India",
      "emoji": "",
      "question": "From 16-December-2019, one can transfer money online using the _____ (NEFT) route 24x7, i",
      "answer": "National Electronic Funds Transfer",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In this role, the RBI focuses on the development and functioning of safe, secure and efficient payment and settlement mechanisms.  Two payment systems National Electronic Fund Transfer (NEFT) and Real-Time Gross Settlement (RTGS) allow individuals, companies and firms to transfer funds from one bank to another.  These facilities can only be used for transferring money within the country.  From 16-December-2019, one can transfer money online using the National Electronic Funds Transfer (NEFT) route 24x7, i. , any time of the day and any day of the week.  The Reserve Bank of India stated earlier in December-2019 that bank customers will be able to transfer funds through NEFT around the clock on all days including weekends and holidays from 16-December.  In RTGS, transactions are processed continuously 24x7"
    },
