      "emoji": "",
      "question": "From 1 July 2020, RBI is offering _____, 2020 (Taxable) – FRSB 2020 (T)",
      "answer": "Floating Rate Savings Bonds",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The RBI also helps the GoI to raise money from the public via issuing bonds and government-approved securities.  In September 2019, a decision at RBI directors meet was taken to change the RBI financial accounting year to March–April to align itself with the central government calendar instead of the current June–July year.  RBI issue taxable bonds for investments.  From 1 July 2020, RBI is offering Floating Rate Savings Bonds, 2020 (Taxable) – FRSB 2020 (T).  The interest on the bonds is payable semi-annually on 1 January and 1 July every year.  The coupon on 1 January 2021 shall be paid at 7.  The Interest rate for next half-year will be reset every six months, the first reset being on 1 January 2021"
    },
    {
      "id": "q4969",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "category": "RBI Press Releases",
      "region": "",
      "source": "Wiki",
      "pubDate": "2026-06-28T13:34:40.588Z",
      "subject": "RBI Press Releases",
      "subSubject": "Reserve Bank of India",
