      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Key tools in this effort include Priority Sector Lending such as agriculture, micro and small enterprises (MSE), housing and education.  RBI work towards strengthening and supporting small local banks and encourage banks to open branches in rural areas to include large section of society in banking net.  === Custodian to foreign exchange === The Reserve Bank has custody of the country's reserves of international currency, and this enables the Reserve Bank to deal with crisis connected with adverse balance of payments position.  === CSD for G-Sec (government securities) === Public Debt Office (PDO) acts as CSD (Central Securities Depository) for G-Sec.  === MIFOR (Mumbai interbank forward offer rate) === With LIBOR cessation in 2021, RBI is set to replace MIFOR with a new benchmark.  MIFOR has LIBOR as one of the components and used in interest rate swap (IRS) markets.  == Demonetisation == === 2016 demonetisation === On 8 November 2016, the Government of India announced the demonetisation of all ₹ 500 and ₹ 1,000 banknotes of the Mahatma Gandhi Series despite being warned by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI)"
