      "answer": "Supreme Court",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " In order to restructure the loans up to ₹150 billion, the expert Committee was tasked with coming up with a sector specific plan for successful resolution of the stressed loans.  The parameters were to include aspects related to leverage, liquidity and debt serviceability.  == Attempt to caution customers against virtual currencies == In April 2018, RBI banned banks from supporting crypto transactions after cases of fraud through virtual currencies were reported.  However, the Supreme Court struck down the ban in March 2020.  Among the reasons cited was that cryptocurrencies were not illegal though unregulated in India.  On June 30, 2025, the RBI directed all banks to use the Financial Fraud Risk Indicator (FRI), a tool developed by the Department of Telecommunications.  The FRI flags mobile numbers linked to fraud in real time, helping banks prevent online financial scams"
