      "fact": " Over 95% of Indian consumers prefer to keep their money in bank accounts, while less than 10% choose to invest in equities or mutual funds, according to a SEBI survey.  As per the Reserve Bank of India (RBI), a significant portion of Indian household financial assets are held in the form of bank deposits.  This is consistent with the traditional preference of Indian households for safe and liquid assets.  == History == === Ancient India === The Vedas, ancient Indian texts, mention the concept of usury, with the word kusidin translated as \"usurer\".  The Sutras (700–100 BCE) and the Jatakas (600–400 BCE) also mention usury.  Texts of this period also condemned usury: Vasishtha forbade Brahmin and Kshatriya varnas from participating in usury.  By the 2nd century CE, usury became more acceptable"
