      "question": "By 2013 the _____ employed 1,175,149 employees and had a total of 109,811 branches in India and 171 branches abroad and manages an aggregate deposit of ₹67,504",
      "answer": "Indian Banking Industry",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " This was the first time an investor was allowed to hold more than 5% in a private sector bank since the RBI announced norms in 2005 that any stake exceeding 5% in the private sector banks would need to be vetted by them.  In recent years critics have charged that the non-government owned banks are too aggressive in their loan recovery efforts in connection with housing, vehicle and personal loans.  There are press reports that the banks' loan recovery efforts have driven defaulting borrowers to suicide.  By 2013 the Indian Banking Industry employed 1,175,149 employees and had a total of 109,811 branches in India and 171 branches abroad and manages an aggregate deposit of ₹67,504. 54 billion (US$700 billion or €610 billion) and bank credit of ₹52,604. 59 billion (US$550 billion or €470 billion).  The net profit of the banks operating in India was ₹1,027"
    },
