      "answer": "Financial Services",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "2 billion) against a turnover of ₹9,148. 59 billion (US$95 billion or €82 billion) for the financial year 2012–13.  Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (Hindi: प्रधानमंत्री जन धन योजना, English: Prime Minister's People Money Scheme) is a scheme for comprehensive financial inclusion launched by the Prime Minister of India, Narendra Modi, in 2014.  Run by Department of Financial Services, Ministry of Finance, on the inauguration day, 1. 5 Crore (15 million) bank accounts were opened under this scheme. 2 million) accounts were opened, with around ₹20,288. 1 billion) were deposited under the scheme, which also has an option for opening new bank accounts with zero balance"
