      "emoji": "",
      "question": "== History == Digital India was launched by the Prime Minister of India, Narendra Modi, on 1 July _____, to connect rural areas with high-speed Internet networks and improve digita",
      "answer": "2015",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " The initiative includes plans to connect rural areas with broadband networks.  Indian Prime Minister Narendra Modi launched the program on 1 July 2015.  The campaign supports other government projects, including BharatNet, Make in India, Standup India, industrial corridors, Bharatmala Sagarmala and Amrit Bharat Station Scheme, Atmanirbhar Bharat.  == History == Digital India was launched by the Prime Minister of India, Narendra Modi, on 1 July 2015, to connect rural areas with high-speed Internet networks and improve digital literacy.  The Digital India program aimed to promote inclusive growth of electronic services, products, manufacturing and job opportunities across the rural areas of India.  The campaign primarily focuses on three key areas: digital infrastructure as a utility for every citizen, governance and services on demand, and digital empowerment of citizens.  == Initiatives == The Government of India's entity Bharat Broadband Network Limited (BBNL) which executes the BharatNet project is the custodian of Digital India (DI) project"
    },
