      "answer": "Pradhan Mantri Gramin Digital",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "24 Crore documents digitally.  It is widely used for Aadhaar, driving licenses, CBSE mark sheets, and COVID-19 certificates.  The platform has been integrated into multiple state government services and private apps.  economictimes === Training === Pradhan Mantri Gramin Digital Saksharta Abhiyan was executed by PMGDisha with an outlay of Rs 2,351. 38 crore with the objective of making 6 crore rural households digitally literate by March 2020.  Pradhan Mantri Gramin Digital Saksharta Abhiyan (abbreviated as PMGDisha) is an initiative under Digital India program, approved by The Union Cabinet chaired by the PM Narendra Modi.  The main objective of the Pradhan Mantri Gramin Digital Saksharta Abhiyan was to make 6 crore people in rural areas across India digitally literate, reaching around 40% of rural households by covering one member from every eligible household"
