      "answer": "Andhra Pradesh",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": " Pradhan Mantri Gramin Digital Saksharta Abhiyan (abbreviated as PMGDisha) is an initiative under Digital India program, approved by The Union Cabinet chaired by the PM Narendra Modi.  The main objective of the Pradhan Mantri Gramin Digital Saksharta Abhiyan was to make 6 crore people in rural areas across India digitally literate, reaching around 40% of rural households by covering one member from every eligible household.  Annual Digital India Summit & Awards were held in 2016.  == E-Cabinet == In 2014, the Andhra Pradesh government was led by Chief Minister N.  Chandrababu Naidu and his Council of Ministers held the first paperless e-Cabinet meeting in the country using the app e-Cabinet.  The ministers accessed the agenda of the Cabinet meeting in electronic form by logging into the app on their laptops or Tabs.  === E-Pragati === E-Pragati, the Andhra Pradesh State Enterprise Architecture, is a framework designed to provide 750 services to over 30 million citizens by integrating 34 departments on a single platform"
