      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The Chalcolithic was an archaeological period characterized by the increasing use of smelted copper. It followed the Neolithic and preceded the Bronze Age. It occurred at different periods in different areas, but was absent in some parts of the world, such as Russia, where there was no well-defined Copper Age between the Stone and Bronze Ages. Stone tools were still predominantly used during this period. The Chalcolithic covers both the early cold working of near-pure copper ores, as exhibited by the likes of the North American Great Lakes Old Copper complex, from around 6,500 BC, through the "
