      "question": "What is Formally independent states, but subordinate to the Roman Empire?",
      "answer": "Client kingdoms in ancient Rome",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "A client kingdom or people in ancient Rome meant a kingdom or ancient people that was in the condition of \"appearing\" still independent, but in the \"sphere of influence\" and thus dependence of the neighboring Roman Empire. It was a form of modern protectorate, where the kingdom or territory in question were controlled or occupied (under the guise of protection) by a stronger power."
