      "question": "_____ was the concert party of the 29th Division, a First World War infantry division within the British Army",
      "answer": "The Diamond Troupe",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The Diamond Troupe was the concert party of the 29th Division, a First World War infantry division within the British Army. Also known as the \"Incomparable Division\", the 29th was formed in 1915 by combining units that had previously been acting as garrisons about the British Empire. The division fought throughout the Gallipoli Campaign and, from 1916 to the end of the war, on the Western Front in France. Concert parties were an integral element of the war effort, and by 1917, virtually every division had at least one. They mirrored the Pierrot troupes of music halls and seaside resorts, offer"
