      "question": "What is German government crisis during World War I?",
      "answer": "Crisis of July 1917",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The crisis of July 1917 was a political crisis experienced by the German Reich between July 7 and 13, 1917. It marked the climax of the conflict between Chancellor Theobald von Bethmann-Hollweg and the German military, which had the backing of Crown Prince Wilhelm. This ended in the military's favor. As a result, the Chancellor's reform program was scrapped, his chief sponsor was dismissed, and a statesman they considered more pliable, Georg Michaelis, was appointed to the top post."
    },
