      "question": "What is Defunct newspaper from Middleton, Idaho, USA?",
      "answer": "Boise Valley Herald",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The Boise Valley Herald, was a small weekly newspaper from Middleton, Idaho that ran from June 14, 1928 to September 26, 1968. In September 1942, The federal government, under Attorney General Francis Biddle, revoked the second-class mailing rights of the Boise Valley Herald. Despite its limited circulation, the paper held significant importance in challenging the \"good war\" narrative of World War II due to its principled stance and the weak justification for its censorship."
