      "fact": "Article 371J of the Constitution of India is a special provision that grants special status to the Kalyana Karnataka region (formerly known as Hyderabad-Karnataka) in the state of Karnataka. It was inserted into the Constitution by the Constitution (Ninety-eighth Amendment) Act, 2012, and came into force on 1 January 2013. The article provides for measures such as reservation in education and employment, and the establishment of a dedicated development board to address regional imbalances."
