      "question": "What is Unwanted effect in clinical chemistry?",
      "answer": "Carryover effect",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The carryover effect is a term used in clinical chemistry to describe the transfer of unwanted material from one container or mixture to another. It describes the influence of one sample upon the following one. It may be from a specimen, or a reagent, or even the washing medium. The significance of carry over is that even a small amount can lead to erroneous results."
    },
