      "fact": "Carbodiphosphoranes are a class of organophosphorus compounds and a subtype of carbones with general formula C(PR3)2, consisting of a central carbon atom bound to two phosphine ligands by dative bonds. The central carbon atom has formal oxidation state zero and two high-energy lone pairs with σ and π-symmetry, making carbodiphosphoranes highly nucleophilic and strongly σ- and π-donating through the carbon atom. Carbodiphosphoranes have gained interest for their unique double-donating properties,"
