      "question": "What is Algorithm for displaying text containing both left-to-right and right-to-left scripts?",
      "answer": "Unicode bidirectional algorithm",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The Unicode Bidirectional Algorithm (UBA), formally defined in Unicode Standard Annex #9 (UAX #9), is a specification developed by the Unicode Consortium that determines how text containing a mixture of left-to-right and right-to-left scripts is displayed. It is a normative part of the Unicode Standard and is required for conformance wherever characters from right-to-left scripts such as Arabic or Hebrew are rendered."
