      "question": "What is Red dye applied to hands and feet during weddings and festivals?",
      "answer": "Alta (dye)",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "Alta (Bhojpuri: 𑂄𑂪𑂞𑂰, Bengali: আলতা), lakshaya rasa, alah, parani, vasantam or mahavar is a red dye mainly used in India, Bangladesh and Nepal to tint the hands and feet as a cultural practice. It is usually applied with a cotton swab or brush during wedding ceremonies and festivals. Natural alta is produced from red lac, although today it is mainly replaced with synthetic dyes."
