      "question": "What is Era of Neo-romanticism in Hindi literature?",
      "answer": "Chhayavad",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "Chhayavad (ISO: Chāyāvād) refers to the era of mystical-romanticism in Hindi literature, particularly poetry, spanning approximately from mid-1910s to early-1940s. It emerged as a reaction to the didacticism of its previous poetic movement - the Dwivedi era - as well as the courtly traditions of poetry."
