      "hint": "",
      "fact": "Buranjis (Ahom language: ancient writings) are the state historical chronicles and manuscripts of the Ahom kingdom (fl. 1228–1826). Although the tradition claims an origin in the 13th century, scholarly research indicates that the written chronicles likely took shape only from the late 14th–16th centuries onward, following the emergence of the Tai Ahom script. The Buranjis were written initially in the Ahom Language and from the 16th century additionally in the Assamese language. The Buranjis are an example of historical literature which is rare in India—they bear resemblance to Southeast Asia"
    },
