      "question": "What is Budhasvāmin's Sanskrit abridgment of the now lost Great Story?",
      "answer": "Bṛhatkathāślokasaṃgraha",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "Bṛhatkathāślokasaṃgraha (Brihat-katha-shloka-sangraha, बृहत्कथाश्लोकसंग्रह), \"Verse Abridgment of the Great Story\", is an abridgement into Sanskrit verse of the now lost Great Story (Bṛhatkathā). It tells the legend of the youthful exploits of prince Naravāhanadatta (Nara-vahana-datta). The poet, Budhasvamin (बुधस्वामिन, also transliterated as Budhasvāmin), is known only through this work."
    },
