      "question": "Eventually, the _____ changed its name to the \"Cuban Nationalist Movement\" (MNC)",
      "answer": "Cuban Nationalist Association",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "The Cuban Nationalist Association (or Cuban Nationalist Organization) was a terrorist organization of Cuban exiles who were responsible for a series of bombings against the Castro regime and the Cuban government. The association was a violent offshoot of the Cuban dissident movement. Eventually, the Cuban Nationalist Association changed its name to the \"Cuban Nationalist Movement\" (MNC). The founder of the organization was Felipe Rivero Diaz."
