      "question": "What is Nigerian climate activist?",
      "answer": "Adedoyin Adeleke",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "Adedoyin Adeleke (born July 7, 1989) is a Nigerian climate change activist and the first African to be appointed a co-chair of the Independent Group of Scientists by the UN Secretary-General, António Guterres on 19 September 2025. He started a climate change program in schools in Africa where students are taught to be positive agents and champions in mitigating climate change in their communities. He is the Director of Green Growth Africa Sustainability Network."
