      "question": "_____s usually generate heat from burning coal and, when in use, have glowing coal or charcoal pieces but few or no flames.",
      "answer": "Angithi",
      "hint": "",
      "fact": "An angithi (Hindustani: अंगीठी or انگیٹھی) is a traditional brazier used for space-heating and cooking in the northern areas of South Asia, mainly in India, Pakistan and Nepal. Angithis usually generate heat from burning coal and, when in use, have glowing coal or charcoal pieces but few or no flames."
